 "id": "T05-deckpegs",
 "title": "Jaw centreline offset at the fingertips vs roll axis (X, closing axis)",
 "mode": "linear",
 "units": "mm (pinch point x vs roll axis, gripper frame G)",
 "requirement": "Pinch point within +/-0.5 mm of its design position, without a per-unit TCP calibration. The systematic shift from finger B lagging by half the design backlash (0.25 * jt0 * L_tip / r) is known and calibrated into the TCP, so the spec is centred on it.",
 "notes": "Rev A chain, roll axis to pinch point: pilot float, horn eccentricity and servo-5 play (T04 terms, X component); spider insert holes to the recess (one print); the deck floats on 4 M3 screws in \u00d83.6 holes (nothing locates it); deck holes to the pin A hole (one PETG housing print, about 30-45 mm apart); knuckle A sleeve on pin A. Pin B follows pin A by the centre distance a (T06, same shared names), so x_B = x_A + a and x_c = x_A + (a - a0)/2: pin A float nets +0.5 (it is +1 in x_A and -1 in a), the A-to-B hole spacing and pin B float enter at 0.5. Dog lash turns A and B by equal and opposite angles, so the centre does not move.",
